---
const details = [
  {
    title: "Dedup on sha256(DER), never serial",
    body:
      "Certificate serial numbers collide across CAs. Merkleye dedups on the SHA-256 hash of the DER-encoded certificate — the one identifier that's actually unique.",
  },
  {
    title: "Punycode/A-label normalization",
    body:
      "IDN homoglyph domains are Unicode, but SAN entries are A-label-encoded on the wire. Comparing Unicode against a wire-format SAN matches nothing and fails silently — everything is normalized to A-label before comparison.",
  },
  {
    title: "Public Suffix List aware",
    body:
      "Phishing certificates live on subdomains. Variant lookups reduce through the PSL to eTLD+1 first, so login.secure-paypaI.com still resolves back to the watched variant.",
  },
  {
    title: "Transparent, additive scoring",
    body:
      "Risk scoring (internal/score) is a documented, additive rule set — not a black-box model. Every score is explainable back to the specific signals that produced it.",
  },
];
---

<section id="correctness" class="border-t border-(--color-border-soft) py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="flex flex-col justify-between gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-end">
      <div class="max-w-xl">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-(--color-accent) uppercase">
          Correctness
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-(--color-ink) sm:text-4xl">
          The details that keep false positives — and false negatives — down.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="max-w-sm text-sm leading-relaxed text-(--color-ink-faint)">
        None of this is glamorous. All of it is the difference between a
        watchtower you trust and one you tune out.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-(--color-border) bg-(--color-border) sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        details.map((d) => (
          <div class="bg-(--color-surface) p-7">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-(--color-ink)">{d.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-(--color-ink-muted)">{d.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
